@startuml activity-forecast
' What happens between clicking "Run forecast" and the numbers appearing.
' No language model is involved anywhere in this diagram.
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg 02-activity-forecast.puml

skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #2F6FB5
skinparam ArrowColor #5B6B7D

|#FDFAF3|You and the app window|
start
:Open the Run screen.
Pick the team, set the "As of" date,
tick "AI narrative" if you want it;
:Click "Run forecast";
note right
  One HTTP request. The window then
  waits for the whole answer, polling
  a progress endpoint once a second.
end note

|#F6FAFF|Forecast service — deterministic Python, no AI here|
:Check the secret token.
Missing or wrong -> HTTP 401, nothing runs;

:1. Load every table: members, teams, tasks,
projects, holidays, vacations, capacity overrides;

:2. Fix the calendar: the two forecast weeks
(Monday-start), the last complete week as the
"origin", and which members count towards workload;

:3. Turn all history into one weekly table —
26 numbers per person per past week;

:4. Backtest: rewind to up to 6 past origins,
two weeks apart, and make all three candidate
models forecast weeks they never saw.
Score each with MASE against what really happened;

:5. Crown the champion — the lowest average score
wins, but only if it is strictly below 1.00.
Otherwise seasonal naive is kept;

:6. Refit the champion on all history and predict
newly arriving hours per person per week;

:7. Effort model — estimate x that person's ratio,
minus the part already done (at least 15 % remains),
spread evenly over their real working days;

:8. Capacity = weekly hours / 5 x surviving working days.
Demand = open hours + new hours.
Overload = max(0, demand - capacity). Demand is never capped;

:9. Low / high band from the champion's own backtest
residuals — 10th and 90th percentile, applied to the
new-arrival half only;

:10. Describe patterns, group similar members and
assemble the facts document;

:Save in ONE transaction:
1 run row + 2 forecast rows per member + 1 facts row;

if (all saved?) then (yes)
  :Reply: run id, both weeks, the champion and
  its score, and every forecast row;
else (no — any write failed)
  :Everything is rolled back. No run row is written,
  so the Runs list never shows a failed forecast;
  stop
endif

|#FDFAF3|You and the app window|
:The two-week totals and the member table appear.
Windows raises a notification naming anyone over capacity;
:Continue in the narrative activity diagram
if the AI narrative was asked for;
stop
@enduml
